      "content": "Clamping each endpoint before connecting it produces incorrect fills when adjacent sessions have opposite signs. For example, +100 followed by −100 draws the profit triangle all the way to the second session and the loss triangle back to the first, rather than having both meet at the halfway break-even crossing. Insert an interpolated zero-crossing point before splitting the positive and negative areas (or clip the original area at break-even), and add a test asserting that both fills meet at that crossing.",
