      "content": "A band can contain multiple partial sales with different same-sign banked amounts, but this selects the latest sale's label and positions it at the first sale's slot and amount. For example, a band stepping from +$478 to +$700 will show “Banked +$700” at the +$478 level and omit the earlier sale's label. Place each banked label using the session that supplies it, or split the band into constant-amount segments before labeling. Add a fixture with two same-sign realizations to cover this case.",
